Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Scale a control line with the column it sits in

Applies on top of [PATCH 1/2] (it uses the column width that patch hands down).

A control line is [label 120][control][CC button 72][LFO handle 30], all fixed,
so it stops shrinking around 300 px. Below that the line does not narrow with
its column: it overflows to the right, over the next column. That is the real
floor on how narrow a band column can be, well above the 120 px clamp, and it
makes the splitter look broken on a column that holds a slider -- the strip
moves, the content does not.

The two widths that are ours to give now scale with the column:

 - side label: 120 px, down to 48 px (clamp(colW * 0.34, 48, 120));
 - MIDI-Learn button: 72 px, down to 36 px (clamp(colW * 0.22, 36, 72));
 - sliders carry an explicit GUILayout.MinWidth(40) instead of inheriting
   EditorGUILayout's own, much larger, minimum.

The upper bounds are the authored values, so a column wide enough for them
renders exactly as before (above roughly 355 px for the label, 327 px for the
CC button). Only narrow columns change, and they change to stay readable
instead of overflowing.

The column width reaches the control lines through _colContentW, set around
each band column in DrawUserTab and -1 outside one, so the full-width area
before the first [Column] keeps the authored sizes.

Package: com.blindspot.kontrols 0.5.1 - Unity 6000.3.10f1
Rationale and known limits: see RAPPORT.md shipped alongside.
NOT yet exercised with a mouse - see "Statut des tests" in RAPPORT.md.
